        <h2 class="color-faint" data-reveal>About</h2>
        <p data-reveal>Hi, I'm Codrin, as in /ko-dreen/.</p>
        <p data-reveal>I've built nearly 100 websites over the last 17 years, mostly for creative agencies and media publishers.</p>
        <p data-reveal>For the past eight years I've focused on annual reports, ESG reports and corporate communications; projects that have won industry awards, received excellent client feedback and launched on time.</p>

        <h2 data-reveal class="mt-6xl color-faint">Communication</h2>
        <p data-reveal>Whether we're in design reviews, development, QA, launch week or post-launch edits, you'll always know what's happening and where the project stands.</p>
        <p data-reveal>I'm probably one of the few frontend developers who actually enjoys keeping project boards tidy. I keep tickets up to date, create missing ones when needed and generally leave the board in a better state than I found it.</p>

        <h2 data-reveal class="mt-6xl color-faint">Working Hours</h2>
        <p data-reveal>I understand agency work isn't always predictable. Early launches happen, clients change their minds, or someone remembers that one last thing on the Friday before launch.</p>
        <p data-reveal>I'm only sometimes surprised when it doesn't happen. I've spent most of my career working US hours from Europe, so late evenings are just part of my routine. I've never missed a deadline.</p>

        <h2 data-reveal class="mt-6xl color-faint">Process</h2>
        <p data-reveal>Every agency has its own way of working and I've become used to adapting. If you already have a process, I'll fit into it. If you don't, that's fine too. I've worked remotely for most of my career, so I self-manage well, communicate proactively and don't need much hand-holding.</p>
        <p data-reveal>I'm equally comfortable working directly with clients or behind the scenes as part of your team—whichever works best for your agency.</p>

        <h2 data-reveal class="mt-6xl color-faint">Budget</h2>
        <p data-reveal>My approach is to find the version of the project that works for you within your client's budget. We'll work together to identify time-intensive features and decide where simplifying, optimising or removing them makes sense. I focus on delivering the best outcome, not the most elaborate implementation.</p>

        <h2 data-reveal class="mt-6xl color-faint">What I'm Looking For</h2>
        <p data-reveal>I do my best work with long-term creative agency partners, especially teams working on annual reports, corporate communications and other content-rich microsites. I enjoy working with detail-oriented designers and content strategists. We tend to care about the same things: clarity, consistency and getting the details right.</p>
        <p data-reveal>If that sounds like your kind of team, I'd love to hear from you.</p>
